WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:27.500
Welcome.  I'm the second Rare Hunter, Pandora.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.750
The illusionist who uses Dark Magician.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.570
You use Dark Magician?

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:38.610
What?

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:46.700
These buzzsaws are used in large-scale magic tricks.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.440
You now know the rules of this duel.

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:51.920
This is fun?

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:56.730
You think it's fun to fight for our lives?

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:59.730
Yes.  Because I'm going to win.

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.610
You're rotten!

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:08.840
I'll show you how a true duelist battles!

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:14.850
Black Magic of the Soul

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:18.590
Dark Magician, attack him directly!

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:21.650
Black Magic!

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:38.830
Pandora, you sliced your cards and cheated.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:43.210
If you continue this game, you will feel the pain that those cards felt.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.960
You still have time to give up!

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:48.150
Give up?  Me?

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.950
I'm having great fun!

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:57.170
Yugi, I'm an illusionist.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:04.520
I want my sole audience member to enjoy my great escape show.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:10.740
An illusionist always has a trick to surprise the audience at the end.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:16.000
I will win this game and escape.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:18.910
You're the one who'll be chopped up.

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:23.280
I no longer have any sympathy for you.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.850
Let's continue the game, Pandora!

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:35.930
Where did Yugi go?

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:39.930
The Ghouls who attacked Jonouchi must be behind this too.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:42.110
We have to find him quickly!

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:46.640
But we have no leads, so where are we supposed to search?

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.670
Continue the duel!

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.610
My turn.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.280
Yugi has Dark Magician on his field.

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:59.550
I can't let it attack me directly on the next turn.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:00.770
Therefore...

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.360
Mystic Tomato in defense position.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:10.590
And I set a card.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:13.530
I end my turn.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:17.260
He only has one defending monster on his field.

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:21.970
On my turn, I'll summon a monster and attack to finish him.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:24.990
Yugi will definitely summon a monster.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:28.410
That's when my Dark Magician will resurrect!

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.200
My turn!

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:35.500
I summon Beta The Magnet Warrior!

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:38.700
I caught him!

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.160
I activate my trap card!

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:41.790
What?  A trap?

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.290
Dark Renewal!

00:04:49.690 --> 00:04:51.970
It takes in summoned monsters.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:05:05.550
Dark Renewal offers our monsters' souls to resurrect Dark Magician's soul from the graveyard.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.990
Resurrect Dark Magician?

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:10.920
Come out, Dark Magician!

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:33.880
Two Dark Magicians are on the field.

00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:37.310
The real battle begins now, Yugi.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:42.880
Since their attack points are equal, neither of us can attack carelessly.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:48.250
Which one of us will use spells and traps to destroy their opponent's Dark Magician first?

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:51.360
That will determine the victor.

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:58.200
I set two more cards this turn.

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:02.670
I end my turn.

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:08.610
Yugi, it seems you know what to do in a battle between Dark Magicians.

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:12.000
My turn.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:15.020
I also set two cards.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:17.120
I end my turn.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.700
My turn.

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:23.430
I set one card and end my turn.

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.130
My turn.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:29.430
I also set one card and end my turn.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.760
My turn.

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:34.350
My turn.

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:38.460
We each have four set cards.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:42.760
I'll get things started.

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:47.200
The spell card Tragedy!

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.190
Is that a guillotine?

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:02.430
Dark Magician!

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:10.600
Yugi, your Dark Magician is finished.

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:17.680
I flip over my spell card Magical Hats!

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:19.650
What?

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:25.960
Magical Hats...

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:27.960
It escaped.

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:31.750
This spell card will find it!  Thousand Knives!

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:38.060
There it is!

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:43.540
How's that?

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:45.130
He found it.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.720
In that case, I use Cursebreaker!

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:56.900
I was so close!

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:59.120
Dark Magician, attack!

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.460
Black Magic!

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:09.250
Both our Dark Magicians are destroyed.

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:12.170
Monster Reborn!

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:23.580
He also had Monster Reborn ready to use.

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:29.390
I applaud you for being evenly matched with my Dark Magician, Pandora.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.310
My turn.

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:33.690
I'm done.

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:36.600
Pandora, you have talent.

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:42.130
A duelist like you must have been a skilled illusionist.

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:47.300
Why would you disgrace yourself by following Marik and becoming the Ghouls' Rare Hunter?

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:51.520
Look at my face.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:57.870
Several years ago, I was at my peak as an illusionist.

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:08.990
I was the most magnificent and famous illusionist in the world.

00:09:09.350 --> 00:09:14.430
And Catherine loved and looked after me.

00:09:29.220 --> 00:09:38.680
But with one failed trick, I lost my fame and Catherine's love.

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:49.310
Lost in despair, I didn't notice Catherine's love for me, even though she supported me.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:53.280
I deeply hurt her emotionally.

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:59.740
When I lost her, I finally realized how much her love meant to me.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:02.960
But it was too late.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:07.800
At my lowest moment, he appeared.

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:21.380
He promised that if I kill you, he'll give me back Catherine's love using his Millennium Rod.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:27.240
Why didn't you trust your supportive girlfriend?

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.600
It's not too late.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.210
You can still talk to her from your heart.

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:35.370
You're still just a kid.

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:37.540
The world is heartless.

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:41.220
Trust won't get you anywhere.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:46.600
Thanks to Marik, Catherine will come back to me.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.590
Catherine is waiting right there.

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:54.900
We'll go back to France together so that we can start over.

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:58.970
Marik, are you also controlling his mind?

00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:04.570
Catherine, I'll bury Yugi so that I can embrace you in my arms again.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:08.040
To accomplish that, I must be heartless.

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:11.510
Duels require trust!

00:11:11.510 --> 00:11:16.480
No matter what happens, I trust my Dark Magician!

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:24.730
The one who believes in himself and his cards to the end will be the victor of this duel!

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:27.300
Yugi, you're too naïve.

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:28.560
We'll see about that.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:33.700
I can see why you're also worthy of being a Dark Magician user.

00:11:34.340 --> 00:11:37.020
But you're forgetting something.

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:42.710
I knew you used Dark Magician before the duel started.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:51.460
So my deck is prepared to thoroughly and heartlessly seal away your Dark Magician.

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:22.530
Yugi, where did you go?

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:47.140
The new Duel Disk System shouldn't work unless it's connected to Kaiba Corporation's main computer.

00:12:47.770 --> 00:12:51.460
But this control room can't find it.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:57.420
If Yugi is dueling a Ghoul, they must be on a different duel system.

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:04.800
Search for Duel Rings in Domino City whose computers are compatible with Duel Disks!

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:13.160
Which of these facilities isn't connected to the main computer and has a basement that blocks all signals?

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:16.030
Big brother!

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:19.530
Big brother, I'll go there.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:36.600
My turn.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:40.130
I set a card.

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:41.730
I end my turn.

00:13:42.810 --> 00:13:43.910
My turn.

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:47.670
I set two cards.

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:49.370
I end my turn.

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:52.490
Here I go.

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:55.130
The spell card Beckon to the Dark!

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:05.420
What's that?

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:15.920
With the spell card Beckon to the Dark, a cursed hand takes your monster into the darkness.

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:18.650
It'll take your Dark Magician!

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:22.600
I won't let you!

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:25.810
The trap card Mystical Refpanel!

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:32.680
This trap card lets me control your spell.

00:14:33.550 --> 00:14:34.930
You fell for it.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:35.670
What?

00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:40.460
It was a decoy to make you use your trap card.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:45.860
This is my real goal!

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:52.170
I can use this trap card when you use a trap card!  Nightmare's Chains!

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:03.550
Dark Magician!

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:13.920
Your Dark Magician can't move and can only watch his master be tortured to death.

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:20.970
Dark Magician is unable to battle, so his attacks will strike my life points directly.

00:15:21.220 --> 00:15:23.220
Are you ready?

00:15:23.220 --> 00:15:26.200
Go, my servant Dark Magician!

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:30.510
Attack him directly!

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:32.440
Black Magic!

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:47.690
Did you like the taste of Black Magic?

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:49.990
It's showtime!

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:55.600
The deadly buzzsaw approaches you!

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:05.840
My magic show is nearing its climax.

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:10.640
When your life points become 0, I will make my escape.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:14.920
The show will end with your blood!

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:17.860
Yugi, it's your last turn!

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:43.180
Even if we keep searching around the city, it'll be impossible to find him.

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:46.180
But if we don't find him, Yugi will be...

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:51.280
Isn't that Mokuba?

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:55.400
Mokuba, it's an emergency.

00:16:55.400 --> 00:16:58.730
Yugi is missing!

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:00.660
Someone must've kidnapped him.

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:02.810
I know where he is.

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:04.600
I'm on the way there.

00:17:05.070 --> 00:17:06.050
Really?

00:17:06.050 --> 00:17:07.700
We'll go with you!

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:09.280
Let's hurry!

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:14.810
I summon Big Shield Gardna in defense position!

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:22.180
I can only try to survive this turn.

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:25.180
Oh, you summoned a monster to protect you.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:30.880
I see.  You're trying to avoid my attack by hiding behind a wall.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:33.290
But it won't work!

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:38.060
Yugi, your life will definitely end this turn!

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:41.510
Are you prepared?

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:43.240
It's my turn.

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:48.820
I'll summon a monster for now.

00:17:49.820 --> 00:17:51.080
Doll of Demise!

00:17:53.020 --> 00:17:57.160
And this is the spell card that will kill you!

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:01.460
The Field Spell Ectoplasmer!

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:04.880
That card is...

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:07.640
You should know it.

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:16.780
This spell card extracts the ectoplasm from a monster and fires it directly at you.

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:18.970
Right past your defending monster.

00:18:19.480 --> 00:18:24.410
No way!  You're willing to sacrifice your monster's soul?

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:27.410
Exactly.

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:31.150
The monster I'm shooting you with will die.

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:37.120
A monster's soul is a small price to pay to win and get Catherine back.

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:39.990
Catherine, I'll be with you soon.

00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:44.160
I'll soon embrace you in my arms.

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:45.770
Please be patient.

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:48.040
Here I go.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:52.710
I'll transform Doll of Demise and Dark Magician into ectoplasm this turn.

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:56.660
Extract ectoplasm!

00:18:59.520 --> 00:19:00.720
Fire!

00:19:11.070 --> 00:19:13.320
One more hit and I'm done.

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:22.700
Yugi, do you know why a fellow Dark Magician user as yourself can't defeat me?

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:24.080
I'll tell you why.

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:27.770
You're not heartless towards your minions.

00:19:28.150 --> 00:19:30.950
Trust is useless.

00:19:31.130 --> 00:19:34.820
You can't win with trust.

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:39.930
Your minion is crucified and can't protect you.

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:47.870
Listen up.  A faithful minion must be willing to give up its life to defeat the enemy.

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:49.300
How dare you!

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:55.620
My Dark Magician must sacrifice itself for its master.

00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:57.320
For my victory.

00:19:57.670 --> 00:20:00.300
Time for the finale.

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:03.470
I activate Ectoplasmer!

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:07.000
Transform Dark Magician into ectoplasm!

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:12.280
Pandora, your monster is crying.

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:16.160
Be quiet!  Fire the ectoplasm!

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:20.370
I win!

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:30.950
What?

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:32.570
Impossible!

00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:34.640
Dark Magician!

00:20:42.650 --> 00:20:47.520
Dark Magician extracted its own ectoplasm?

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:59.100
Dark Magician, you did this for me?

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:08.840
I chose Dark Magician as the monster capable of transforming into ectoplasm this turn.

00:21:09.270 --> 00:21:13.210
That means his Dark Magician could transform as well.

00:21:13.770 --> 00:21:20.150
But I can't believe a card used its own will to extract its ectoplasm and defend the player!

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:24.100
You can't win by being heartless!

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:27.090
I'll prove that to you, Pandora!

00:21:39.600 --> 00:21:44.040
Dark Magician sacrificed itself and barely saved Yugi.

00:21:44.040 --> 00:21:49.020
But Pandora's continuous attacks have him backed against a wall!

00:21:49.170 --> 00:21:53.000
To deal the final blow, Pandora summons a second Dark Magician.

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:57.620
But Yugi's deck doesn't contain another Dark Magician to face it!

00:21:57.620 --> 00:22:02.310
What?  Dark Magician has a student?

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:06.600
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Magician's Student
Dark Magician Girl

00:22:06.770 --> 00:22:08.220
Duel, standby!

00:22:22.260 --> 00:22:26.760
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:27.560 --> 00:22:32.130
I feel like I've been here

00:22:32.670 --> 00:22:41.810
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:42.110 --> 00:22:53.320
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:56.190 --> 00:23:00.830
Time passes bit by bit

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:06.100
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:06.670 --> 00:23:11.210
Will never change

00:23:11.870 --> 00:23:16.480
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:17.110 --> 00:23:21.680
To be who I am

00:23:22.280 --> 00:23:26.920
I've kept searching for something

00:23:27.590 --> 00:23:31.630
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:34.560
I learned that's the answer

00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:41.670
From now until forever...
